# The proven legacy PyAC corpus.
#
# These are the sentence vectors the VLIW/PyAC pack encoder is proven against.
# They keep the legacy declaration spelling `su name <name> ob ... ya`, because
# the named-literal codelet has no slot for the `exists` keyword and a pack
# round-trip has to reproduce the original sentence exactly.
#
# The runtime example in examples/pyash/pyac-corpus.pya uses the `exists`
# spelling, because the interpreter requires it to create a name. The two files
# therefore differ in exactly those three lines, and the difference is the
# honest one: the pack vector proves the encoding, the example proves the
# interpreter.

ob num 1 to num 1 be plus do
ob num 9 from num 4 be subtract do
ob num 3 with num 4 be multiply do
ob num 8 with num 2 be divide do
ob num 7 to num 3 be xor do
ob num 7 be number ya
ob text "Pyash" be text ya
ob bool truth ya
su name collector ob num 7 be number ya
su name collector ob text "A" be text ya
su name collector answer ob bool lie ya
ob text "opaque" to name collector be plus do
ob num 2 be invert do
ob num 2 from num 3 be exponential do
ob num 9 from num 4 be remains do
exists su name values ob ve num 1 2 3 be vector ya
exists su name start ob date 2025-05-01 be date ya
